 127: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
 128:     """
 129:     Paint the maze corridor and framed rooms lying on shortest paths between the two colored endpoint components.
 130: 
 131:     Input structure
 132:     - The grid has a dominant background, one wall color forming thin orthogonal frames, and one endpoint/fill color.
 133:     - The endpoint/fill color forms exactly two 4-connected solid rectangular components; their larger side lengths define the framed room sizes.
 134: 
 135:     Rule
 136:     - Treat wall pixels as blocked and every other pixel as passable.
 137:     - Find every passable pixel that lies on a shortest 4-connected path between the two endpoint components.
 138:     - Also fill any framed square room of an endpoint-derived size that intersects that shortest-path mask.
 139: 
 140:     Key insight
 141:     - Shortest paths identify the route through open connector corridors, while the wall-bordered square rooms need to be expanded from the route centerline to their full interior.
 142:     """
